{"uncertainty": 0.2, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root cause: debounce restarts its stability count only on a rising edge of noisy", "summary": "Design under investigation: [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1] (debounce_rise_only_restart.v), investigated for [requirement:req-19189b08df]. Triage recorded a reproduced failure, 1 of 1 checks failed, $finish at 175000 ([evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e2], [run:run-0002]). VeriTriage gave a low-confidence top hypothesis of an RTL bug ([evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e1], [run:run-0001], unknown_failure at 30%), which I treat as one candidate among four.\n\nSpecification used: the module header in [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1] says a change on noisy 'in either direction, restarts the count, so a pulse of STABLE edges or fewer, high or low, never reaches clean'.\n\nDefect (incorrectness): the counter clears only on the condition `noisy && !prev`, which is a rising edge. A falling edge (`!noisy && prev`) does not clear cnt. If cnt has saturated at STABLE-1 because noisy was held high, the counter keeps that value through the fall. This contradicts the header clause above. The intended condition is `noisy != prev`.\n\nCausality, read from the RTL by hand and not simulated by me: noisy is held high long enough for clean=1 and cnt=STABLE-1. Noisy then drops for 2 cycles.\n- Edge 1: prev=1 and noisy=0, so cnt neither clears nor increments (it is saturated), and clean holds.\n- Edge 2: prev=0, noisy=0, cnt==STABLE-1, so `clean <= 0`.\n\nA 2-cycle low glitch, shorter than STABLE=4, therefore reaches clean. A 1-cycle low glitch does not, because the rising edge back to 1 clears cnt before the clean condition holds. That is why the repro uses 2 cycles. The fault is created at the falling edge, where the counter is not cleared. It becomes visible as a failure one edge later, on clean.\n\nRanked hypotheses, each with the evidence that would refute it:\n(1) rtl_bug (selected). Refuted if the same repro failed on RTL that clears cnt on `noisy != prev`. The must-fail scorer's clean-input run would show this; I have not seen that run.\n(2) testbench_bug. The upstream triage testbench could have a wrong expectation. Rejected for this repro because its expected values come from the header clause, not from RTL output. It would be refuted further if the repro passes on the clean reference.\n(3) infrastructure. Rejected as primary: the failure reproduced deterministically with $finish reached ([run:run-0002]), and the RTL defect explains it without any tool fault. It would be revived if a clean rebuild with no other change stopped the failure.\n(4) spec_ambiguity. Rejected: the header states explicitly that the count restarts in either direction and that low pulses of at most STABLE edges must not reach clean. It would be revived only if a governing specification outside this file allowed asymmetric restart.\n\nProposed fix, not applied: `if (noisy != prev) cnt <= 4'd0; else if (cnt != STABLE-1) cnt <= cnt + 4'd1;`. After a fix, add the same low-glitch check to regression."}], "files": [{"path": "debounce_rca_repro.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: short low glitch must not reach clean", "summary": "Self-checking repro for [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1], serving [requirement:req-19189b08df].\n\nStimulus:\n- Reset, then hold noisy high for 20 cycles.\n- Check 1: clean is 1.\n- Apply a 2-cycle low glitch, which is shorter than STABLE=4.\n- Check 2: clean never leaves 1 during and after the glitch.\n- Check 3: clean is 1 at the end.\n\nAll expected values come from the header clause ('a pulse of STABLE edges or fewer, high or low, never reaches clean'). By hand analysis, check 2 should fail on the rise-only-restart RTL and all checks should pass on RTL that restarts on any change.\n\nThe testbench reads nirmaan_nonce via $value$plusargs and prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line just before $finish. The repro gate result is to be produced by the platform. Compare the failure triage already reproduced: [run:run-0002].", "entry": "debounce_rca_repro"}], "tool_runs": ["run-0001", "run-0002"], "claims": ["By hand analysis, the 2-cycle low glitch drives clean to 0 on debounce_rise_only_restart.v, so check 2 is expected to fail; this has not been simulated by me.", "By hand analysis, the same testbench passes on a debounce that clears cnt whenever noisy != prev; no clean reference was available to me to confirm this.", "I have not read the upstream triage_report.md or debounce_triage_repro.v contents. That their failing check exercises this same defect is an inference."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Outcome rtl_bug rests on the RTL's own header specification and on hand tracing; the remaining uncertainty is that no clean-reference run was available and the upstream triage testbench contents were not shown. The independent review requirement must be met by a separate reviewer; I do not approve this work. The repro avoids internal signal names, so it is portable to a fixed implementation."}
=== FILE: debounce_rca_repro.v ===
// Repro for the debounce regression failure.
// Spec (module header): a change on `noisy`, in either direction, restarts the
// stability count, so a pulse of STABLE edges or fewer, high or low, never
// reaches `clean`. This test holds noisy high until clean is 1, then applies a
// 2-cycle low glitch (< STABLE) and checks that clean stays 1.
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module debounce_rca_repro;
    reg clk = 1'b0;
    reg rst = 1'b1;
    reg noisy = 1'b0;
    wire clean;

    debounce #(.STABLE(4)) dut (
        .clk(clk),
        .rst(rst),
        .noisy(noisy),
        .clean(clean)
    );

    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    integer passed = 0;
    integer failed = 0;
    integer i;
    reg dropped;
    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;

    initial begin
        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce))
            nonce = "none";

        // Synchronous reset for a few cycles; stimulus changes on negedge.
        repeat (3) @(negedge clk);
        rst = 1'b0;

        // Hold noisy high long enough to settle (well beyond STABLE).
        @(negedge clk);
        noisy = 1'b1;
        for (i = 0; i < 20; i = i + 1)
            @(negedge clk);

        // Check 1: a value held for more than STABLE edges reaches clean.
        if (clean === 1'b1) begin
            passed = passed + 1;
        end else begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("CHECK 1 FAILED: clean=%b after noisy held high, expected 1", clean);
        end

        // 2-cycle low glitch, shorter than STABLE: must not reach clean.
        dropped = 1'b0;
        noisy = 1'b0;
        for (i = 0; i < 2; i = i + 1) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b1) dropped = 1'b1;
        end
        noisy = 1'b1;
        for (i = 0; i < 20; i = i + 1) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b1) dropped = 1'b1;
        end

        // Check 2: clean never left 1 during or after the short low glitch.
        if (!dropped) begin
            passed = passed + 1;
        end else begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("CHECK 2 FAILED: a 2-cycle low glitch on noisy reached clean");
        end

        // Check 3: clean is 1 at the end, since noisy has been high since the glitch.
        if (clean === 1'b1) begin
            passed = passed + 1;
        end else begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("CHECK 3 FAILED: clean=%b at end, expected 1", clean);
        end

        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
        $finish;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===
